The "Deeply Personal Software" Licence

Let's be honest with each other. If I kept Lattice closed, you'd point an agent at the binary,
decompile it and reimplement it by teatime; that's how good agents have got. I'll save you
the bother: here's the source. Take it, change it, make it yours. Go and make software that
works for you.

And that's the one thing I ask: make it yours. Lattice is customised for me, its audience of
one. If you build on it, especially to sell, shape it for your own audience and your own market,
and give it your own name and face. Don't hand people my software with the serial numbers filed
off.

The paragraphs above are the spirit. The terms below are the letter: the MIT licence, word for
word, with one condition added about Lattice's name and the things that make it mine.

